/*!
@defgroup dma_driver
@ingroup mod_system Direct Memory Access (DMA)
@brief Hardware DMA engine driver for the YTMicro SDK.

@details
The DMA module provides a multi-channel direct memory access engine that
performs complex data transfers with minimal CPU intervention. The driver
abstracts the DMA hardware into a virtual channel model, supporting
single-block, multi-block, loop, and ram-reload (scatter-gather) transfer
modes.

@section dma_features Key Features
- Memory-to-memory, peripheral-to-memory, memory-to-peripheral, and
  peripheral-to-peripheral transfer types.
- **Single-block transfer** — one contiguous buffer transferred in a single
  DMA request.
- **Multi-block transfer** — a buffer divided into blocks, each transferred
  upon a separate DMA request.
- **Loop transfer** — configurable transfer/trigger loop counts with
  source/destination address offsets and channel linking.
- **Ram reload (scatter-gather)** — automatic CTS descriptor chaining for
  complex multi-segment transfers.
- Dynamic virtual channel allocation across multiple DMA instances.
- Per-channel callback on transfer completion or error.
- Configurable address modulo for circular buffer support.
- Transfer sizes from 1 byte to 64 bytes per read/write.
- Half-complete and full-complete interrupt support.
- Optional ECC error detection (device-dependent).

@section dma_arch Module Architecture

@verbatim
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│               Application Code                   │
│          (calls DMA_DRV_* functions)             │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│       DMA Driver Layer (dma_driver.h/c)          │
│  ● Virtual-channel-based API                     │
│  ● Transfer configuration helpers                │
│  ● Channel lifecycle (init / release / start)    │
│  ● Callback management                           │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│    DMA HW Access Layer (dma_hw_access.h/c)       │
│  ● Direct register-level CTS manipulation        │
│  ● Module control (halt, cancel, error flags)    │
│  ● Mostly inline functions for performance       │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│       DMA IRQ Layer (dma_irq.h/c)                │
│  ● Interrupt vector routing per platform         │
│  ● Dispatches to DMA_DRV_IRQHandler()            │
├──────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          DMA / DMAMUX Peripheral Hardware        │
│     (CTRL, CTS[], CHMUX[], status registers)     │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
@endverbatim

@subsection dma_arch_driver Driver Layer (dma_driver.h)
Application code should **only** use the `DMA_DRV_*` functions. These accept
a zero-based **virtual channel** index and internally resolve the DMA instance
and hardware channel.

@subsection dma_arch_hw HW Access Layer (dma_hw_access.h)
Internal layer providing low-level register accessors, organized into groups:
- **Module Initialization** — DMA_Init(), DMA_CancelTransfer(), DMA_SetHaltOnErrorCmd()
- **Module Configuration & Control** — DMA_SetTransferLoopMappingCmd(), DMA_SetDmaRequestCmd(), interrupt flags
- **CTS Source Configuration** — DMA_CTSSetSrcAddr(), DMA_CTSSetSrcOffset(), modulo, transfer size
- **CTS Destination Configuration** — DMA_CTSSetDestAddr(), DMA_CTSSetDestOffset(), etc.
- **CTS Transfer Loop & Trigger** — DMA_CTSSetNbytes(), DMA_CTSSetTriggerCount(), channel linking
- **CTS Ram Reload & Interrupt** — DMA_CTSSetRamReloadLink(), half/full complete interrupts
- **DMAMUX** — DMAMUX_Init(), DMAMUX_SetChannelSource()

@section dma_config Configuration Parameters

@subsection dma_config_user dma_user_config_t Fields
| Field              | Type   | Description                                                                  |
|--------------------|--------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| haltOnError        | bool   | If true, any error sets HALT — all subsequent requests are ignored until cleared. |
| eccErrorEnable     | bool   | Enable ECC error detection (only when `FEATURE_DMA_SUPPORT_ECC_ERROR_CHECK == 1`). |
| maxChannelForChLink| bool   | Enable errata E406002 workaround using the last channel for link clearing.   |

@subsection dma_config_channel dma_channel_config_t Fields
| Field           | Type                  | Description                                              |
|-----------------|-----------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| virtChnConfig   | uint8_t               | Virtual channel number to allocate.                      |
| source          | dma_request_source_t  | Peripheral DMA request source routed through DMAMUX.     |
| callback        | dma_callback_t        | User callback invoked on transfer complete or error.     |
| callbackParam   | void *                | Opaque parameter passed to the callback.                 |

@subsection dma_config_transfer dma_transfer_config_t Fields
| Field                   | Type                          | Description                                                         |
|-------------------------|-------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| srcAddr                 | uint32_t                      | Source start address.                                               |
| destAddr                | uint32_t                      | Destination start address.                                          |
| srcTransferSize         | dma_transfer_size_t           | Source read size per bus access (1/2/4/8/16/32/64 bytes).           |
| destTransferSize        | dma_transfer_size_t           | Destination write size per bus access.                              |
| srcOffset               | int16_t                       | Signed offset added to source address after each read.              |
| destOffset              | int16_t                       | Signed offset added to destination address after each write.        |
| srcLastAddrAdjust       | int32_t                       | Source address adjustment at trigger loop completion.                |
| destLastAddrAdjust      | int32_t                       | Destination address adjustment at trigger loop completion.           |
| srcModulo               | dma_modulo_t                  | Source address modulo (circular buffer mask, `DMA_MODULO_OFF` = disabled). |
| destModulo              | dma_modulo_t                  | Destination address modulo.                                         |
| transferLoopByteCount   | uint32_t                      | Bytes transferred per DMA request (transfer loop count).            |
| ramReloadEnable         | bool                          | Enable ram reload (scatter-gather) for this descriptor.             |
| ramReloadNextDescAddr   | uint32_t                      | Address of next CTS descriptor (must be 32-byte aligned).           |
| interruptEnable         | bool                          | Generate interrupt when trigger loop count reaches zero.            |
| loopTransferConfig      | dma_loop_transfer_config_t *  | Pointer to loop configuration (NULL if not using loop mode).        |

@subsection dma_config_loop dma_loop_transfer_config_t Fields
| Field                       | Type     | Description                                                        |
|-----------------------------|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------------|
| triggerLoopIterationCount   | uint32_t | Number of trigger loop (major) iterations.                         |
| srcOffsetEnable             | bool     | Apply transfer loop offset to source address on loop completion.   |
| dstOffsetEnable             | bool     | Apply transfer loop offset to destination address on loop completion.|
| triggerLoopOffset           | int32_t  | Signed offset applied to src/dest after transfer loop completes.   |
| transferLoopChnLinkEnable   | bool     | Enable channel linking on transfer loop (minor) completion.        |
| transferLoopChnLinkNumber   | uint8_t  | Channel number linked on transfer loop completion.                 |
| triggerLoopChnLinkEnable    | bool     | Enable channel linking on trigger loop (major) completion.         |
| triggerLoopChnLinkNumber    | uint8_t  | Channel number linked on trigger loop completion.                  |

@subsection dma_config_features Device Feature Macros
| Macro                                   | Description                                             |
|-----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|
| FEATURE_DMA_CHANNELS                    | Number of hardware channels per DMA instance.           |
| FEATURE_DMA_VIRTUAL_CHANNELS            | Total virtual channels across all DMA instances.        |
| FEATURE_DMA_SUPPORT_ECC_ERROR_CHECK     | Set to 1 if ECC error detection is available.           |
| FEATURE_DMA_ERRATA_E406002              | Set to 1 if errata workaround is needed.                |
| FEATURE_DMA_ENGINE_STALL               | Defined if DMA engine stall cycles are configurable.    |
| FEATURE_DMAMUX_AVAILABLE                | Defined if DMAMUX peripheral is present.                |

@section dma_usage Usage Patterns

@subsection dma_usage_single Pattern 1: Single-Block Memory-to-Memory Transfer
Transfer a contiguous buffer between two memory locations in a single DMA
request.

@code{.c}
#define DMA_VIRT_CHN  (0U)

dma_state_t dmaState;
dma_chn_state_t chnState;
dma_chn_state_t *chnStateArray[] = { &chnState };

dma_channel_config_t chnConfig = {
    .virtChnConfig = DMA_VIRT_CHN,
    .source        = DMA_REQ_DISABLED,
    .callback      = dmaCallback,
    .callbackParam = NULL
};
const dma_channel_config_t *chnConfigArray[] = { &chnConfig };

dma_user_config_t userConfig = {
    .haltOnError = false
};

uint8_t srcBuffer[256];
uint8_t destBuffer[256];

/* Step 1: Initialize DMA module and channel */
DMA_DRV_Init(&dmaState, &userConfig, chnStateArray, chnConfigArray, 1U);

/* Step 2: Configure single-block transfer (M->M, 4 bytes per access, 256 bytes total) */
DMA_DRV_ConfigSingleBlockTransfer(DMA_VIRT_CHN, DMA_TRANSFER_MEM2MEM,
                                   (uint32_t)srcBuffer, (uint32_t)destBuffer,
                                   DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_4B, sizeof(srcBuffer));

/* Step 3: Start channel — transfer begins on first DMA request */
DMA_DRV_StartChannel(DMA_VIRT_CHN);

/* Step 4: Trigger a software request to start immediately */
DMA_DRV_TriggerSwRequest(DMA_VIRT_CHN);

/* Transfer complete callback will fire when done */
@endcode

@subsection dma_usage_multi Pattern 2: Multi-Block Peripheral-to-Memory Transfer
Receive data from a peripheral register (e.g., UART RX) in multiple blocks,
one block per DMA request.

@code{.c}
#define DMA_VIRT_CHN  (1U)
#define UART_RX_DATA  (0x4006A00CU)  /* Example UART data register address */

uint8_t rxBuffer[64];

/* After DMA_DRV_Init() and DMA_DRV_ChannelInit()... */

/* Configure: P->M, 1 byte per access, 8 bytes per block, 8 blocks, disable request on completion */
DMA_DRV_ConfigMultiBlockTransfer(DMA_VIRT_CHN, DMA_TRANSFER_PERIPH2MEM,
                                  UART_RX_DATA, (uint32_t)rxBuffer,
                                  DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_1B,
                                  8U,   /* blockSize: 8 bytes per request */
                                  8U,   /* blockCount: 8 blocks = 64 bytes total */
                                  true); /* disable request after completion */

DMA_DRV_StartChannel(DMA_VIRT_CHN);
/* Each UART RX request transfers 8 bytes; after 8 requests, callback fires */
@endcode

@subsection dma_usage_loop Pattern 3: Loop Transfer with Address Offsets
Use transfer/trigger loop configuration for advanced addressing, such as
transferring rows of a matrix with a stride.

@code{.c}
#define DMA_VIRT_CHN  (2U)

dma_loop_transfer_config_t loopConfig = {
    .triggerLoopIterationCount = 4U,        /* 4 trigger loop iterations */
    .srcOffsetEnable           = false,
    .dstOffsetEnable           = false,
    .triggerLoopOffset         = 0,
    .transferLoopChnLinkEnable = false,
    .transferLoopChnLinkNumber = 0U,
    .triggerLoopChnLinkEnable  = false,
    .triggerLoopChnLinkNumber  = 0U
};

dma_transfer_config_t transferConfig = {
    .srcAddr                = (uint32_t)srcData,
    .destAddr               = (uint32_t)destData,
    .srcTransferSize        = DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_4B,
    .destTransferSize       = DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_4B,
    .srcOffset              = 4,
    .destOffset             = 4,
    .srcLastAddrAdjust      = -16,  /* Reset source back to start after 4 words */
    .destLastAddrAdjust     = 0,
    .srcModulo              = DMA_MODULO_OFF,
    .destModulo             = DMA_MODULO_OFF,
    .transferLoopByteCount  = 16U,  /* 16 bytes per request */
    .ramReloadEnable        = false,
    .ramReloadNextDescAddr  = 0U,
    .interruptEnable        = true,
    .loopTransferConfig     = &loopConfig
};

/* After DMA_DRV_Init() and DMA_DRV_ChannelInit()... */
DMA_DRV_ConfigLoopTransfer(DMA_VIRT_CHN, &transferConfig);
DMA_DRV_StartChannel(DMA_VIRT_CHN);
@endcode

@subsection dma_usage_ramreload Pattern 4: Ram Reload (Scatter-Gather) Transfer Chain
Chain multiple transfer descriptors together. Each descriptor is automatically
loaded from RAM when the previous one completes.

@code{.c}
#define DMA_VIRT_CHN  (3U)
#define CTS_COUNT     (3U)

uint8_t sctsBuffer[SCTS_SIZE(CTS_COUNT)];
uint8_t src1[32], src2[32], src3[32];
uint8_t dest1[32], dest2[32], dest3[32];

dma_ram_reload_list_t srcList[CTS_COUNT] = {
    { .address = (uint32_t)src1, .length = 32U, .type = DMA_TRANSFER_MEM2MEM },
    { .address = (uint32_t)src2, .length = 32U, .type = DMA_TRANSFER_MEM2MEM },
    { .address = (uint32_t)src3, .length = 32U, .type = DMA_TRANSFER_MEM2MEM }
};
dma_ram_reload_list_t destList[CTS_COUNT] = {
    { .address = (uint32_t)dest1, .length = 32U, .type = DMA_TRANSFER_MEM2MEM },
    { .address = (uint32_t)dest2, .length = 32U, .type = DMA_TRANSFER_MEM2MEM },
    { .address = (uint32_t)dest3, .length = 32U, .type = DMA_TRANSFER_MEM2MEM }
};

/* After DMA_DRV_Init() and DMA_DRV_ChannelInit()... */
DMA_DRV_ConfigRamReloadTransfer(DMA_VIRT_CHN,
                                 (dma_software_cts_t *)sctsBuffer,
                                 DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_4B,
                                 32U,       /* bytesOnEachRequest */
                                 srcList, destList, CTS_COUNT);
DMA_DRV_StartChannel(DMA_VIRT_CHN);
DMA_DRV_TriggerSwRequest(DMA_VIRT_CHN);
/* After each trigger completes, the next CTS is loaded automatically.
   Callback fires only after the last CTS completes. */
@endcode

@section dma_api API Quick Reference

@subsection dma_api_init Initialization & De-initialization
| Function              | Description                                                     |
|-----------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_Init()        | Initialize DMA module, state structure, and optional channels.  |
| DMA_DRV_Deinit()      | De-initialize DMA module and release all channels.              |

@subsection dma_api_chn Channel Management
| Function                  | Description                                                 |
|---------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_ChannelInit()     | Initialize a virtual channel (allocate, set source, callback). |
| DMA_DRV_ReleaseChannel()  | Release a virtual channel and free its resources.           |

@subsection dma_api_config Transfer Configuration
| Function                            | Description                                                  |
|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_ConfigSingleBlockTransfer() | Configure a single contiguous block transfer.                |
| DMA_DRV_ConfigMultiBlockTransfer()  | Configure a multi-block transfer with trigger loop.          |
| DMA_DRV_ConfigLoopTransfer()        | Configure transfer with full loop control (offsets, linking).|
| DMA_DRV_ConfigRamReloadTransfer()   | Configure a ram reload (scatter-gather) descriptor chain.    |
| DMA_DRV_PushConfigToReg()           | Copy a transfer config structure to CTS hardware registers.  |
| DMA_DRV_PushConfigToSCTS()          | Copy a transfer config structure to a software CTS in RAM.   |
| DMA_DRV_CancelTransfer()            | Cancel the currently executing transfer.                     |

@subsection dma_api_ctrl Channel Control
| Function                                | Description                                              |
|-----------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_StartChannel()                  | Enable DMA requests for the virtual channel.             |
| DMA_DRV_StopChannel()                   | Disable DMA requests for the virtual channel.            |
| DMA_DRV_SetChannelRequestAndTrigger()   | Configure the DMAMUX request source for a channel.       |
| DMA_DRV_ClearCTS()                      | Clear all CTS registers to zero for a channel.           |
| DMA_DRV_TriggerSwRequest()              | Trigger a software DMA request on a channel.             |

@subsection dma_api_src Source Address Configuration
| Function                            | Description                                              |
|-------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_SetSrcAddr()               | Set source address for a channel CTS.                    |
| DMA_DRV_SetSrcOffset()             | Set signed source address offset per read.               |
| DMA_DRV_SetSrcReadChunkSize()      | Set source data read size (1/2/4/8/16/32 bytes).         |
| DMA_DRV_SetSrcLastAddrAdjustment() | Set source address adjustment at trigger loop completion. |

@subsection dma_api_dest Destination Address Configuration
| Function                             | Description                                               |
|--------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_SetDestAddr()                | Set destination address for a channel CTS.                |
| DMA_DRV_SetDestOffset()              | Set signed destination address offset per write.          |
| DMA_DRV_SetDestWriteChunkSize()      | Set destination data write size (1/2/4/8/16/32 bytes).    |
| DMA_DRV_SetDestLastAddrAdjustment()  | Set destination address adjustment at trigger loop completion. |

@subsection dma_api_loop Transfer Loop Configuration
| Function                                     | Description                                                |
|----------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_SetTransferLoopBlockSize()           | Set bytes transferred per DMA request (transfer loop).     |
| DMA_DRV_SetTriggerLoopIterationCount()       | Set number of trigger loop (major) iterations.             |
| DMA_DRV_GetRemainingTriggerIterationsCount() | Get remaining trigger loop iterations.                     |
| DMA_DRV_SetRamReloadLink()                   | Set next CTS descriptor address for ram reload.            |
| DMA_DRV_DisableRequestsOnTransferComplete()  | Disable or enable requests after trigger loop completion.  |

@subsection dma_api_int Interrupt & Callback
| Function                      | Description                                                   |
|-------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_ConfigureInterrupt()  | Enable/disable error, half-complete, or complete interrupts.  |
| DMA_DRV_InstallCallback()     | Register or unregister a callback for a virtual channel.      |

@subsection dma_api_status Status
| Function                    | Description                          |
|-----------------------------|--------------------------------------|
| DMA_DRV_GetChannelStatus()  | Get current status of a DMA channel. |

@section dma_notes Important Notes

@subsection dma_notes_clock Clock Dependency
The DMA peripheral clock must be enabled via the @ref clock_manager **before**
calling DMA_DRV_Init(). The driver does not manage clocks internally.

@subsection dma_notes_vchan Virtual Channel Mapping
Virtual channels map linearly across DMA instances. If a device has 2 DMA
modules with 32 channels each, virtual channels 0-31 map to DMA0 and 32-63
map to DMA1. Use virtual channel numbers consistently across all driver API
calls.

@subsection dma_notes_alignment Address Alignment
- Source and destination addresses **must** be aligned to the transfer size.
  For example, a 4-byte transfer requires 4-byte-aligned addresses.
- Ram reload CTS descriptors **must** be 32-byte aligned. Use the SCTS_SIZE()
  and SCTS_ADDR() macros to allocate and align properly.

@subsection dma_notes_modulo Modulo (Circular Buffer) Usage
When using the modulo feature, the application must ensure the buffer start
address is aligned to a power-of-2 boundary equal to the modulo size. The
modulo value freezes the upper address bits, creating a circular address
range.

@warning Misaligned modulo buffers produce undefined transfer results.

@subsection dma_notes_periph Peripheral Transfer Size Constraint
For peripheral-to-memory or memory-to-peripheral transfers, the transfer
size **must** match the peripheral data register width:
- 8-bit data register: use `DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_1B`.
- 32-bit data register: use `DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_4B`.

@warning Using a mismatched transfer size causes truncated data transfers.

@note In L/Z series devices, `DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_16B` and
`DMA_TRANSFER_SIZE_32B` are **not** supported.

@subsection dma_notes_irq Interrupt Priority
The driver enables DMA channel and error interrupts internally, but does
**not** configure interrupt priorities. The application must set appropriate
priorities using the interrupt manager.

@section dma_integration Integration Guide

@subsection dma_integration_files Compilation Units
The following source files must be added to the project build:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/dma/dma_driver.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/dma/dma_hw_access.c
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/src/dma/dma_irq.c
@endverbatim

@subsection dma_integration_include Include Paths
Add the following directory to the toolchain include path:
@verbatim
${SDK_PATH}/platform/drivers/inc/
@endverbatim

@subsection dma_integration_symbols Compile Symbols
No special compile-time symbols are required. Device-specific feature macros
(`FEATURE_DMA_*`, `FEATURE_DMAMUX_*`) are defined automatically in the
device features header.

@subsection dma_integration_deps Dependencies
- @ref clock_manager — Required for enabling the DMA peripheral clock.
- @ref interrupt_manager — Required for enabling DMA channel interrupts.

*/
